WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:03.260
Hey youtubers, what’s up.

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:07.290
It’s time for a new Game of Thrones Bonus
video and since we haven’t been North in

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.870
a long time I wanted to do a video for Mance
Rayder.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.460
The season 4 episodes they’re screening
in IMAX also feature the Wall a lot.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:16.240
So this will mostly be a history video from
the books going up to the end of Book 5.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:21.760
I’ll just add a spoiler tag when I get to
stuff they might be doing in Season 5.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.300
Just to make it easier to follow I’ll bounce
back and forth between book stuff and show

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:26.300
stuff.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.860
The show didn’t use him that much, so it’s
not really that big a deal.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:34.210
I’ll add current Season 5 news and giveaway
stuff at the end.

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:39.489
I will be talking about fan theories, so just
assume spoiler theories for Mance.

00:00:39.489 --> 00:00:43.479
Most of the evidence is conjecture taken from
offhanded comments george rr martin and cast

00:00:43.479 --> 00:00:45.730
members have made as well as subtext from
the books.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:47.190
So here we go,

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:51.319
Most of you probably already guessed I was
talking about the theory Mance is secretly

00:00:51.319 --> 00:00:52.739
a glamoured Rhaegar Targaryen.

00:00:52.739 --> 00:00:57.050
I don’t think it’s true because Mance
gets glamoured in book 5.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:00.899
And to the best of my knowledge, you can’t
double glamour someone.

00:01:00.899 --> 00:01:03.510
Add to that, the glamouring process required
a jewel.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.250
A physical device that he had to keep attached
to himself to maintain his new appearance.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:12.010
So if Mance had been Rhaegar all along, when
he had been stripped of his posessions after

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:13.010
being captured.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:16.900
His appearance would have changed immediately.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:23.570
And based on the way the actor is playing
it on the show, Mance’s motivations are

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:24.720
very simple and genuine.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.900
He wants to keep the wildlings from getting
slaughtered by the white walkers.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:35.720
I just wanted to start with that so we could
all be on the same page when talking about

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:36.820
Mance’s history.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:41.780
Even though very little is known about his
life before joining The Night’s Watch.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:43.430
That’s really where his recorded history
starts.

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:49.750
He was born a wildling north of the wall and
as a child got caught up in a random raiding

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.240
party that tried to attack the Night’s Watch.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:55.960
Everyone was killed but the Brothers showed
Mance mercy and gave him the chance to take

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:57.181
the Black or be put to the sword.

00:01:57.181 --> 00:02:01.170
So that’s how Mance ended up in the Night’s
Watch, which he remained until adulthood.

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:05.040
He claims he visited Winterfell more than
once, the first time being while he was still

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:06.040
wearing The Black.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:07.360
Mance’s Lord Commander was Qorgyle.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.890
He traveled to Winterfell sometime in the
early years after Robert’s Rebellion to

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:12.549
meet with Ned Stark.

00:02:12.549 --> 00:02:25.230
Probably to ask for more support, more supplies.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:56.030
At the time Mance claims he saw a very young
Robb Stark and Jon Snow.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:03.769
The second time he claims to have visited
was during the night Robert Baratheon visited

00:03:03.769 --> 00:03:06.310
Ned Stark to offer him the job as Hand of
The King.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:12.379
That’s the very beginning of Book 1.

00:03:12.379 --> 00:03:20.180
Mance claims he disguised himself as a musician
and played in the dining hall.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:23.639
That time he was running recon.

00:03:23.639 --> 00:03:31.499
He’d already united the Wildling Groups
and was trying to gauge the threat level from

00:03:31.499 --> 00:03:34.519
King Robert, Ned and Benjen Stark.

00:03:34.519 --> 00:03:37.510
Probably because he was in the early days
of planning to migrate the wildlings south

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:38.510
of the wall.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:42.309
But at the time he had no idea how any of
them would react.

00:03:42.309 --> 00:03:47.559
Benjen he called a “bane” to the wildlings.

00:03:47.559 --> 00:03:57.579
I think Mance was hoping he’d find them
reasonable people.

00:03:57.579 --> 00:04:02.120
So rewind back in the timeline a little.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:09.370
The reason Mance abandoned the Night’s Watch
is kind of a twist on the Jon Snow Ygritte

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:10.370
relationship.

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:13.340
He was out Ranging North of the Wall one day
and a shadowcat almost killed him.

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:17.780
A random wilding woman found him, healed him
and patched up his torn cloak.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:24.170
The books don’t specify, but it sounds like
he was with her for a moderate amount of time.

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:25.170
Enough to form a connection.

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:27.270
It wasn’t an overnight thing.

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:30.690
When he came back to the Night’s Watch,
Qorgyle disciplined him for not replacing

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:34.940
the cloak the Wildling Woman had patched and
I that became the straw that broke the camel’s

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:35.940
back.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:39.320
Mance’s time with the Wildling Woman had
reminded him of the freedom he’d lost serving

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.900
in the Night’s Watch and said peace, I’m
outta here and returned to the free folk.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:45.270
While he was a brother he was primarily stationed
at the Shadow Tower.

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:46.390
That’s the one right here.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:47.960
In the books Denys Mallister is the commander
there.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:51.520
Side Note: There was an actor who was going
to play Mallister on the show.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:52.520
But he died four days into filming Season
5.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:53.520
He is important to the story, but they never
said how they would work around the issue.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:54.520
I think what they’ll do is just use a few
of his scenes and then for the rest of his

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:55.520
story, just have Jon Snow and the other characters
refer to him in third person.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.640
It’s also possible they completely re-wrote
his arc and gave his lines to Alliser Thorne

00:04:57.640 --> 00:04:58.640
and Janos Slynt.

00:04:58.640 --> 00:04:59.660
The timeline is a little fuzzy on how many
years passed between Mance’s first visit

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:00.660
to Winterfell and the moment he abandoned
his post.

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:01.660
As well as the moment he became King of the
Wildlings.

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:02.660
We don’t even know his true age.

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:04.630
The books describe him as having grey hair,
so I’d say he’s Older than Ned Stark by

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:06.170
several years.

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:08.460
If Ned were still alive.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:11.610
But much much younger than Jeor Mormont.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:13.410
So maybe late 40s.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:19.350
The funny thing about character ages is that
the tv show made most of the adult characters

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:23.310
older than they are in the books.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:25.050
Jaime and Cersei are a good example.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.500
In the books they’re much younger.

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:31.900
You have to remember during this period, just
like in real life history.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:34.790
People got married and had children much much
younger.

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:37.720
Cersei was 18 in the books when she married
Robert.

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:39.430
Joffrey was born two years after that.

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:43.700
So right now where we are in the story, she’s
mid 30s.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:45.880
On the show, she’s closer to mid 40s.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:51.300
They fudge things like that, I don’t think
the tv show has ever said explicitly how old

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.300
everyone is.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:57.300
But they come of as being comparable to the
actual age of the Actors.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:00.830
Given all that, I think Mance was born less
than 10 years before Ned Stark.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:02.900
During Book 1, he’s described as showing
signs of premature grey.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:04.390
Looking way older than he actually is.

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:06.320
And Mance’s grey hair is totally normal.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:10.400
Most recently in the books, Mance led the
failed attempt to take The Night’s Watch.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:17.900
I believed him when he said he only wanted
to save his people.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:20.150
Stannis is at The Wall and Mance is in captivity
awaiting judgement.

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:22.460
Because some of you might not have read the
books yet.

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:29.250
I’ll put the spoiler tag up here while I
talk about him in Book 5.

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:31.320
So here we go, important stuff.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:37.820
Mance at the Wall, does not end up in the
fire.

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:39.730
Why did Melisandre save him?

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:45.490
I’m sure there were several reasons, mostly
being he’s a very capable leader of men

00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:47.580
with expansive knowledge of the North.

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:51.070
He’s going to be a big asset in their war
with the white walkers.

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:55.980
Second reason, his blood might not qualify
as Royal enough to satisfy Melisandre's spell

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:57.570
to raise a dragon.

00:06:57.570 --> 00:07:09.370
The 
books don’t get super explicit on what qualifies

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:11.230
as Royal Blood.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:19.890
Mance’s son qualified, so maybe you have
to be born a Royal.

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:26.540
Regardless, I think just in general Melisandre
felt like killing Mance would hurt their cause

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:27.840
more than it would help it.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:32.050
So as of right now he’s still alive, albiet,
glamoured to look like Rattleshirt.

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:37.660
I think he’ll continue to give them advice
as the white walkers descend on the wall in

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:38.660
the next two books.

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:39.660
I’m just going to avoid talking about Jon
Snow’s role in all this, because he’s

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:41.560
